From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:29:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] build: run a link's LTO jobs one after another

Packages link with -flto=auto. As a package's build does not pass make's
jobserver on to the compiler, GCC then runs as many LTRANS jobs at once
as the host has CPUs, beside the other packages make builds at the same
time, and their diagnostics interleave line by line in the package's
log: a warning can follow another job's chain of inlined calls and be
placed in the wrong function, or lose its function, so the warnings of
one build differ from the next.

Run each link's LTRANS jobs one after another (-flto=1). The partitions
stay the same, as their number follows GCC's parameters, not the number
of jobs, and the build stays parallel through make, which builds several
packages at once.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [wrt-build reads GCC's warnings from each package's build log]
---
 include/package.mk | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/package.mk b/include/package.mk
index 823a055..507d2aa 100644
--- a/include/package.mk
+++ b/include/package.mk
@@ -55,9 +55,9 @@ ifeq ($(call pkg_build_flag,gc-sections,$(if $(CONFIG_USE_GC_SECTIONS),1,0)),1)
   TARGET_LDFLAGS+= -Wl,--gc-sections
 endif
 ifeq ($(call pkg_build_flag,lto,$(if $(CONFIG_USE_LTO),1,0)),1)
-  TARGET_CFLAGS+= -flto=auto -fno-fat-lto-objects
-  TARGET_CXXFLAGS+= -flto=auto -fno-fat-lto-objects
-  TARGET_LDFLAGS+= -flto=auto -fuse-linker-plugin
+  TARGET_CFLAGS+= -flto=1 -fno-fat-lto-objects
+  TARGET_CXXFLAGS+= -flto=1 -fno-fat-lto-objects
+  TARGET_LDFLAGS+= -flto=1 -fuse-linker-plugin
 endif
 ifdef CONFIG_USE_MOLD
   ifeq ($(call pkg_build_flag,mold,1),1)
